# Project 6

## AI Medical Diagnosis System

### Description

The AI Medical Diagnosis System was a Python-based project that introduced me to the concept of **rule-based expert systems**, one of the earliest forms of Artificial Intelligence. The objective of the project was to design a system capable of suggesting possible diseases based on symptoms entered by the user.

Unlike machine learning models that learn patterns from data, this system relied on predefined medical rules and logical decision-making to produce its diagnoses. The project demonstrated how knowledge can be represented and processed using conditional statements and inference rules, providing a practical introduction to symbolic AI.

### What I Did

During this project, I completed the following tasks:

- Designed a knowledge base containing symptoms and their associated diseases.
- Created rule-based diagnosis logic using conditional statements.
- Developed a command-line interface (CLI) that allows users to interact with the system.
- Processed user input and validated the entered symptoms.
- Implemented an inference process to match symptoms with possible diseases.
- Displayed diagnostic suggestions based on the rules defined in the knowledge base.
- Organized the program into reusable functions to improve readability and maintainability.

### Skills Learned

This project helped me develop practical skills in Artificial Intelligence and Python programming, including:

- Rule-based expert systems
- Knowledge representation
- Logical reasoning
- Decision-making algorithms
- Python programming
- Conditional logic
- User input handling
- Command-line application development
- Program organization and modular design

### Challenges

The primary challenge of this project was designing logical diagnosis rules that produced meaningful and consistent results. Since the system relied entirely on predefined knowledge rather than learning from data, each rule had to be carefully constructed to avoid incorrect or conflicting diagnoses.

Another challenge was organizing the code so that new diseases and symptoms could be added without significantly modifying the existing program. This required thinking about scalability and maintainability while keeping the logic clear and easy to understand.

### Outcome

This project provided valuable insight into how expert systems function and demonstrated that Artificial Intelligence is not limited to machine learning. I learned how knowledge can be represented using rules and how logical inference can be used to solve practical problems.

The experience strengthened my Python programming skills and introduced me to symbolic AI concepts, preparing me for more advanced intelligent systems that combine rule-based reasoning with machine learning techniques.
